<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Gemex raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Gemex raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman Brothers analyst Will Landers said he raised his rating on Grupo Embotellador de Mexico SA de CV (Gemex) to outperform from neutral.</p>
<p>-- He set a 12-month price target of $15 per American Depositary Receipt (ADR).</p>
<p>-- &quot;The company recorded strong operating margin performance in the first quarter of 1997, when operating income grew 118 percent and the operating margin expanded from 4.9 percent in the first quarter of 1996 to 11.3 percent in the first quarter of 1997,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- The company's ADRs closed Friday at 11.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
